measure`) with breakpoints at 1100/1600/2000/2560px — de-cramping is a\n  matter of retuning these + the base type scale, not new structure.\n\n## Implementation\n\n### 1. New offline organic 2D renderer — `widgets/force_graph_2d/`\n- `vendor/force-graph.module.js` — the `force-graph` (2D, non-React) ESM dist, vendored. Obtain\n  once via `npm install force-graph` then copy `dist/force-graph.mjs` into `vendor/` (a one-time\n  fetch at implementation time; **runtime stays fully offline**). Pin the version in a short\n  `vendor/README.md`.\n- `index.js` — `createForceGraph2DRenderer(options)` implementing the `{mount, update, dispose}`\n  contract, mirroring `three_renderer`'s lifecycle (sync handle returned immediately; lazy\n  `import()` of the **local** vendor path via an injectable `options.loader`; updates before load\n  replayed on activation; `dispose` cancels a pending activation). Reuse the same\n  `layoutToGraphData(layout, physics)` normaliser shape (export a shared one or copy it) so\n  `fluid` = organic motion.\n  Port memo-ray's paint from `OrganicGraph.jsx`: earth-tone `PALETTE`, node glow, rust-red\n  highlight + pulse ring, `linkColor`/`linkWidth`/`linkDirectionalParticles` for the active path,\n  `nodeCanvasObject` labels above zoom 1.2, and the corner **minimap** canvas. Honour the existing\n  `onNodeClick`/`onNodeHover` callbacks and `focusedLayer`/filter predicates the widgets pass.\n- `force_graph_2d.css` — container + minimap styling (mirror the inline styles from OrganicGraph,\n  themed via `--ps-*`/`--color-*` tokens).\n- Test: `tests/widgets_force_graph_2d_test.mjs` — copy the structure of\n  `widgets_three_renderer_test.mjs` (fake host, stubbed `loader`, lifecycle + layout-normalising\n  assertions). No network.\n\n### 2. Make organic 2D the default in the Bridge — `bridge.js`\n- Add `makeForceRenderer(physics = \"fluid\")` returning `createForceGraph2DRenderer({...})`, pointed\n  at the local vendor path.\n- Memory: pass `{ renderer: this.makeForceRenderer() }` into `createLineageGraphWidget`\n  (`bridge.js:781`) so the living graph replaces the static SVG by default.\n- Documents/Code: invert the current 3D-opt-in. Default renderer = `makeForceRenderer`; the\n  `docs3d`/`code3d` toggles swap in `makeThreeRenderer` instead. SVG remains the final fallback if\n  the vendor import fails (renderer returns the inline-error handle, like three_renderer does).\n- Keep `pinned`/`fluid` physics wired to the existing `docsPhysics`/`codePhysics` toggles.\n\n### 3. Navigable breadcrumbs — `view.html` + `bridge.js` + `bridge.css`\n- `bridge.js`: a computed `crumbs()` built from `{ mode, workspace, selection }`. Selection state\n  already exists per mode (`activeSessionId`, `activeRun`/`activeStepId`, selected doc/graph node);\n  expose a single normalized `selectionLabel`/`selectionId`. Path shape:\n  **Bridge › {Mode} › {Workspace} › {Selection}**. Add `goCrumb(crumb)` that, by level, switches\n  mode / resets workspace scope / clears the active selection (e.g. `selectSession(null)`).\n- `view.html`: replace the bare `ps-bridge__stage-bar` (workspace `<select>` only, `view.html:109`)\n  with a breadcrumb bar that contains the crumb trail **and** the workspace selector, so the bar\n  earns its space and the cockpit feels integrated rather than bolted-on. Crumbs are `<button>`s\n  with `aria-current=\"page\"` on the last (WCAG structure + keyboard operable).\n- `bridge.css`: `.ps-bridge__crumbs` styling (sage separators `›`, muted ancestors, solid current),\n  hover/focus-visible states.\n\n### 4. De-cramp spacing & type — `bridge.css`\n- Base type up to the 16px baseline: `.ps-bridge { font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.5 }`; `h3`\n  13→15px; list subs 12→13px; status/tagline 12→12.5px.\n- More breathing room at the base breakpoint: `--ps-gap` 32→40, `--ps-stage-pad` 14→20, top-level\n  `.ps-bridge` padding 18/22→24/28, shell `gap` 14→18; rail item padding `9px 11px`→`11px 14px`\n  with `gap` 4→6; panel `gap` 14→18;