---\n\nStarted 2026-06-22. Reworking the Prime-Silo **Bridge cockpit** (`app/L0/_all/mod/_prime_silo/bridge/` — single Alpine.js view: view.html / bridge.js ~1326 lines / bridge.css) plus the **Space Agent auth screens**. Driven by the [[make-project-right]] design contract (zen earth-tone palette; canonical tokens; no cool-neons).\n\n**Operator scoping decisions (locked):**\n- Auth rebrand scope = **full Space Agent retheme** (not just login).\n- Token strategy = **canonical colors.css** (single source of truth, mirror via aliases — make-project-right rule 9).\n- Build order = **Bridge 4K layout FIRST**, then the rest.\n\n**Phase 3 — memo-ray parity (2026-06-24, code done, NOT browser-verified):** addressed operator feedback \"Bridge feels like an add-on, no breadcrumbs, cramped, want memo-ray's living graphs.\" Three changes:\n1. **Organic 2D graph is now the cockpit default** (Memory + Documents + Code); 3D (three_renderer) is the opt-in toggle. New offline renderer `widgets/force_graph_2d/` ports OrganicGraph.jsx's look (force motion, glow, rust-red `#db533f` highlight + pulse, animated trace particles on the active link path, corner minimap, earth-tone PALETTE). Same `{mount,update,dispose}` + `layoutToGraphData(layout,physics)` seam as three_renderer; supports pinned (fx/fy frozen) vs **fluid (organic, now the default** — flipped `docsPhysics`/`codePhysics` \"pinned\"→\"fluid\"). `fireClick` prefers `props.onSelect` over factory `onNodeClick` to avoid double-fire. `bridge.js` `makeForceRenderer()` wired into all three mount sites; physics (Fluid/Rigid) toggle de-gated from 3D-only.\n2. **Offline graph lib** — vendored `force-graph@1.51.4` as a self-contained esbuild ESM bundle at `force_graph_2d/vendor/force-graph.module.js` (0 bare imports; loaded via relative `import.meta.url`, NO CDN). Rebuild recipe in `vendor/README.md`. (Contrast three_renderer = esm.sh CDN.)\n3. **Navigable breadcrumbs** — `crumbs` getter (Bridge › Mode › Workspace › Selection) + `goCrumb`/`clearSelection` in bridge.js; breadcrumb bar replaces the workspace-only stage-bar in view.html (last crumb `aria-current`, ancestors clickable to clear drill-in). **De-cramp**: base font 14→15.5px + line-height 1.5; `--ps-gap` 32→40, `--ps-stage-pad` 14→20, rail/panel/list padding up; breakpoint type scale fixed to grow monotonically (1600 was setting 15px < new base). Cache-bust bumped `bridge.css?v=6`→`v=7`; added force_graph_2d.css link.\n- **Verified offline:** new `tests/widgets_force_graph_2d_test.mjs` + lineage/synoptic/three_renderer/bridge_page/bridge_context/bridge_command tests all green; eslint clean; vendor bundle valid ESM. Pre-existing unrelated red still `bridge_documents_test::testIngestPushesWorkspace`. NOT browser-verified (needs `desktop:localtest` shell+runtime to see live graphs).\n\n**Phase plan:**\n- **Phase 0 — Bridge 4K layout** (IN PROGRESS). Done: (1) Bridge now loads canonical `_core/framework/css/colors.css` and its `--ps-*` tokens are mirrors of the canonical `--color-*` palette w/ literal fallbacks; (2) layout tokens (`--ps-rail-w/--ps-benny-w/--ps-gap/--ps-stage-pad/--ps-measure`) + scale-up breakpoints at 1600/2000/2560px; (3) **multi-pane split view** — opt-in secondary \"Observe\" pane (run lineage timeline + reasoning trace) beside the primary mode, only ≥1600px. Tracked in `_widgets2`/`mountSecondary`/`observeRun`, mounts into `obsTimeline`/`obsTrace` refs so a primary mode switch never tears it down. Code done, NOT browser-verified (needs running shell+runtime).\n- **Phase 1 — Studio/notebooks** (DONE, native). New `studio` mode = cell-based notebook: Chat cells → `/rag/chat`, Report cells → `/deep-produce` (poll). Chose native reuse (NOT open-notebook) for a self-contained testable build. `studioCells[]` + `runStudioCell`/`pollStudioCell`/`openStudioCellTrace`. MODES now 8 (added studio; bridge_page_test updated 6→8, order: pulse,memory,documents,code,flows,studio,runs,agents).\n- **Phase 2 — Observability** (DONE). Wired in `drilldown_table` (Steps chips → `/pypes/runs/{run}/steps/{step}`); live poll toggle (`startRunPoll`, 3s, refreshes timeline/trace/drilldown while run non-terminal); real metrics strip (status/duration/steps/failed/errors from RunRecord — NO fabricated cost/tokens, RunRecord lacks them; future: aggregate `/governance/events`). Linked run-widget CSS (was unstyled). `frame_inspector` NOT yet wired (needs a frame object source). `runFlow`/deep-produce-trace route into Observe pane when split active.\n- **Build**: `npm run desktop:pack` (fast shell-only) builds clean → `dist/desktop/windows/win-unpacked/Space Agent.exe`. Gotcha: build EBUSY-fails if Space Agent.exe is running (locks win-unpacked) — quit it first. Live Studio/Runs data needs a Benny runtime (shell-only pack has none; use `desktop:localtest` for the zero-install bundled runtime).\n- **Pre-existing unrelated red test** (NOT mine): `bridge_documents_test::testIngestPushesWorkspace` — expects old `ingest()` body; ingest() now requires selected files.\n- **Phase A — Auth retheme**: `server/pages/login.html` (+ enter.html, share_space.html — they share `res/space-backdrop.*`) deliberately SKIN-OVERRIDE the canonical earth-tone tokens with a blue space theme (`#050816`/`#7ddcff`) = the rule-9 \"Skin Override\" anti-pattern. Fix ≈ delete the blue `:root`, inherit canonical palette, swap floating astronaut → **Benny** (asset already exists: `app/L0/_all/mod/_core/visual/res/chat/overlay/dog_no_bg.svg`, \"Benny the floating German Shepherd\", earth-tone), strip/zen-ify the star backdrop.\n\n**CRITICAL root-cause for \"whole screen wasted on 4K\" (fixed 2026-06-22):** the Bridge opens as a router PANEL (`bridge/ext/panels/bridge.yaml`, route path `_prime_silo/bridge`), mounted same-document (no iframe) into `.router-route-mount`. `_core/router/router.css` caps EVERY routed panel at `.router-stage-inner { width: min(100%, 84rem); margin: 0 auto }` — a centred 1344px reading column. Only the `spaces` route escapes the cap. **First attempt FAILED**: I keyed an override on `.router-stage-inner[data-route-path=\"_prime_silo/bridge\"]`, but `router-store.js mount()` is called with only `{ outlet, viewport }` (see router/view.html) — `refs.stageInner` is UNDEFINED, so `.router-stage-inner` NEVER gets a `data-route-path` attribute. (`spaces` only LOOKS like it uses that selector; it actually goes full-width via a `width:100vw; margin-left:calc(50% - 50vw)` breakout in `spaces.css` `.spaces-view-root`.) **Working fix (in bridge.css, NOT router.css):** `.ps-bridge { width:100vw; max-width:100vw; margin-left/right: calc(50% - 50vw); min-height: calc(100vh - var(--router-shell-start-clearance,43px)); }` — escapes the 84rem column + claims full height. Put it in bridge.css because that file is cache-busted (`?v=6`) and proven to load fresh; router.css is NOT cache-busted (stale-cache risk). This is why the internal responsive/token CSS looked like it \"did nothing\" — the host column stayed 1344px. NOT a space-widget (widgets dirs empty); `openPanel` just routes.\n\n**Workspace dropdown only showed \"default\" (fixed 2026-06-22):** runtime_proxy.js `buildUpstreamUrl` = `base + \"/api\" + trimmed` where trimmed = path minus `/api/runtime`. So `runtimeFetch(\"/workspaces\")` → `8005/api/workspaces` (CORRECT — returns `[\"default\",\"prime_silo_self\"]`). DON'T add `/api` yourself (→ `8005/api/api/...` 404 — a wrong turn I made and reverted). `readRuntimeJson` = simple JSON.parse (handles arrays fine). Real cause = COLD-START RACE: `loadWorkspaces` fires once on mount, fire-and-forget; if runtime still booting it 404s and never retries → stuck on [\"default\"]. Fix: kept `/workspaces` path + added retry (attempt<5, 1.5s) + string|{id} shape tolerance. Pre-existing, unrelated to layout work.\n\n**Gotcha:** edit only the canonical `app/L0/...` source — there are regenerated mirror copies under `.benny_home/workspaces/`, `home/workspaces/`, `packaging/self-awareness/source/` that must NOT 